Not by Demogoron (was wearing an AoLS when he got me), though an arch-
lich decided to invite Yeenoghu and Demogorgon over for a family get-
together. Not by Rodney, who showed up approximately ten times (was
wearing several different AoLS). The nasties simply waged a war of
attrition. Thus my Sporkhack high score simply reads: killed by a
stalker.

220 HP and -17AC is nowhere *near* sufficient for a combat wombat. I
guess since I've never ascended a true wombat, preferring casters, I
didn't realize that even with a +5 ring of increase damage and +7
Grayswandir, my character was still too wimpy to ascend.

There aren't too many highlights, other than a ridiculously easy early
game thanks to good armor and two magic lamps, a middle game made
much, much easier by the spellbook of detect treasure (no need to
explore a level if it only brings you an iron skull cap!), a
reasonably easy descent through Gehennom, and an ascension run from
hell.

I attempted a genoless game. Most everything fell in two or three hits
from my +5 increase damage / +7 Grayswandir combo. But when an
annoyingly non-genocided arch-lich retreated to the stairs during the
ascension run, and I was but three squares away, he decided to have a
demon party.

A Yeenoghu and Demogorgon party.

Despite cure sickness at 0%, I lost two amulets of life saving during
the encounter as I fumbled through my bag for my *unspent* wand of
wishing, and asked the great RNG to kindly bequeath a cockatrice
corpse. Statues of an arch-lich, Yeenoghu, and Demogorgon: check.

Just after my cockatrice corpse rotted, I encountered Baalzebub,
Rodney, and Rodney, who stole my mitre of holiness and amulet of
Yendor. Sure, I (eventually) killed them, but it wasn't until thirty-
or-so levels upwards that I realized the theft. I've never had the
wizard steal my stuff, lucky me! Well, anyway, I descended, killing
several Rodneys in the process, got my stuff, and received six brain-
sucks from a master mind flayer as punishment for not putting my hat
back on (it had recently been pilfered by yet *another* Rodney), after
which I forgot the scroll of charging.

By the planes, I had run out of death zaps, and my last amulet versus
horrible death crumbled to dust as I exhausted my last wish for a
blessed wand of death.

I've never ascended a wombat, but I still feel I did many things
*right* during the ascension.
First, since amulets and wands are so common in hell, I collected
useless amulets and wands, and whenever I had about five amulets and
ten wands, I polypiled for amulets of life saving and wands of
teleportation. I burned approximately eight amulets during the run.

Those wands of teleportation, even those with two or three charges,
saved my life on numerous occasions. A mind flayer cannot suck your
brains out from the other end of the cavern.
On several occasions, I broke a wand of teleportation, scattering
nasties and saving my life.

I also had Cure Sickness at 0%. With Demogorgon on my tail, this was
easily a lifesaver.

But I didn't buff up my character enough to play him as a wombat, or
polypile/alchemize *nearly*  enough potions of full healing. My next
priest, if I play one again, is going to level himself to exp30 with
graveyard wraiths and rely on magic missile, because I utterly *hate*
using melee attacks in the late game.



